WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:04.213
♫ And the home of the

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.676
♫ brave ♫

00:00:10.031 --> 00:00:11.054
- Pretty good harmony!

00:00:11.054 --> 00:00:12.097
- Not bad.
- Yeah, that was real good.

00:00:12.097 --> 00:00:14.474
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:17.810
- Baseball!

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.887
Here we are at P3.

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:21.397
- Our friend Rodney hooked us up

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:23.691
with this amazing sports science facility.

00:00:23.691 --> 00:00:25.468
- We're going to put you guys
through some testing today

00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:26.690
that we would put any pro baseball

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.112
athlete through, actually.

00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:29.238
- I played Little League baseball

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:31.156
up until about fourth grade.

00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:32.783
The pitching started getting faster

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:34.034
and I got scared.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.953
- [Voiceover] I never got
to the level of baseball

00:00:35.953 --> 00:00:38.247
where another human
throws the ball at you.

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:39.326
- Coming into this,

00:00:39.326 --> 00:00:41.458
I am coming in like a baseball virgin.

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:45.052
- I have never swung a bat. I mean--

00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:48.674
- I'm the only one of use
that even plays sports,

00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:50.510
and now I got a broken,

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.844
I can't even participate.

00:00:51.844 --> 00:00:54.471
- I don't think I've ever
held a mitt, honestly.

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:57.141
- Just, just terrible, just horrible.

00:00:57.141 --> 00:00:58.434
- Cool!

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.561
- The goal for today is
to not sprain anything.

00:01:00.561 --> 00:01:02.304
- I just want to come
out of here in one piece.

00:01:02.304 --> 00:01:03.605
- This is the wrong hand.

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:04.732
- [Voiceover] It goes on,
if you're right-handed.

00:01:04.732 --> 00:01:06.400
- Oh! Ah!

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.486
- It's going to be a fun one!

00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:11.155
- Almost everything we do in baseball,

00:01:11.155 --> 00:01:12.782
we're going to start off
with a lateral stance.

00:01:12.782 --> 00:01:14.616
We're going to look at
how much horizontal force

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:16.078
that we can create.

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:21.332
We want to see how much
lateral drive you guys have,

00:01:21.332 --> 00:01:23.375
and then how much you can actually apply

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:25.377
in a sport-specific baseball manner.

00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:26.876
- So you guys have seen them
make a video game before?

00:01:26.876 --> 00:01:27.963
Same technology.

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:29.769
- We're going to get, like,
motion tracking on us.

00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:31.398
- Benny, hit the lights. Boom.

00:01:31.398 --> 00:01:32.414
- What!

00:01:32.414 --> 00:01:33.635
- [Voiceover] That's so cool!

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:35.156
- So basically all force plates are,

00:01:35.156 --> 00:01:36.680
they're high-tech scales.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.278
They tell us how much force

00:01:38.278 --> 00:01:39.462
you're going to be putting into the ground

00:01:39.462 --> 00:01:41.185
in real time as you go
through any movements.

00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:42.978
- (mumbles) rate, all that kind of stuff.

00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:43.939
- Everything.

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:45.147
- I feel like a superhero.

00:01:45.147 --> 00:01:46.899
- We're going to see,
standing on this plate,

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:48.442
pushing off your back foot,

00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:49.985
how far out can you go.

00:01:49.985 --> 00:01:51.028
- [Voiceover] Go, Keith, go!

00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:52.071
Go, Keith, go!

00:01:52.071 --> 00:01:53.948
- All right, 6.78 for Keith.

00:01:53.948 --> 00:01:55.199
- What's a good number?

00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:57.025
- Think big, baby, think big!

00:01:58.625 --> 00:01:59.787
- Look at that face, Ned.

00:01:59.787 --> 00:02:01.664
- That's 6.9.

00:02:01.664 --> 00:02:02.906
- Yes!

00:02:02.906 --> 00:02:04.247
- The average baseball
player is putting up

00:02:04.247 --> 00:02:06.210
a little over 9 Newtons per kilogram.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.186
So you're a little below that.

00:02:09.186 --> 00:02:11.683
- So how are we going
to succeed on the field?

00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.966
- It's got to be the "it" factor.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.906
- The computer can't tell that.

00:02:14.906 --> 00:02:15.969
- [Woody] Base running, you have to wait

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.221
until the guy hits the ball.

00:02:17.221 --> 00:02:19.223
In this case with a left-handed
pitcher on the mound,

00:02:19.223 --> 00:02:20.391
since he's facing you,

00:02:20.391 --> 00:02:21.809
you're not sure if he's
throwing to the plate

00:02:21.809 --> 00:02:23.185
or he's trying to pick you off.

00:02:23.185 --> 00:02:24.353
- [Keith] Oooh!

00:02:24.353 --> 00:02:25.437
- So we're going to run
through a couple of scenarios

00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:26.981
where he's either going
to throw it to home,

00:02:26.981 --> 00:02:28.273
and you're going to try to steal,

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:29.358
or he's going to try to pick you guys off,

00:02:29.358 --> 00:02:31.026
you guys got to try to dive back in safe.

00:02:31.026 --> 00:02:34.640
- I'm excited, in that sort
of fear-driven excitement.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.781
- You know I don't really pose a threat,

00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:37.341
so why waste a pitch?

00:02:38.161 --> 00:02:39.451
- Ah!

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.454
- I'm giving him the "steal" signal.

00:02:43.364 --> 00:02:45.457
- [Voiceover] Steal,
steal, steal, steal, steal!

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:47.918
- Oh!

00:02:48.615 --> 00:02:49.878
- [Voiceover] Keith, you're out.

00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:51.338
- [Voiceover] Hand up, man, hand up.

00:02:51.338 --> 00:02:52.631
- My doctor would kill me.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:54.383
- [Voiceover] Go!

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.223
- When we talk about baseball,

00:03:03.223 --> 00:03:06.583
it's just a drop-dead rotational
ballistic power sport.

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:08.022
This machine is going to measure

00:03:08.022 --> 00:03:10.483
how much rotational power
that you guys can create.

00:03:10.483 --> 00:03:12.484
So let's just warm it
up nice and easy, okay.

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:13.778
Remember, outside hand on the first,

00:03:13.778 --> 00:03:16.196
inside hand, step away,
feel the resistance,

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.448
pick up your front foot.

00:03:17.448 --> 00:03:18.782
We're going to swing it around.

00:03:22.262 --> 00:03:23.246
- Goddammit, Eugene.

00:03:23.988 --> 00:03:26.874
- Peak power for you, Eugene, 1,062.

00:03:27.249 --> 00:03:28.654
- I feel like if I make a
warrior grunt when I do it,

00:03:28.654 --> 00:03:29.703
it will help.

00:03:29.703 --> 00:03:31.139
- [Woody] Let's see.
- Arrrghh!

00:03:31.139 --> 00:03:32.504
- 761!

00:03:33.297 --> 00:03:35.632
- Feels about right compared
to our physical fitness.

00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:38.761
- The average for pro
baseball is around 2,300.

00:03:38.761 --> 00:03:39.595
- Damn!

00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:41.180
- No matter what this number is,

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.175
we also have to be able to
apply that to a moving ball.

00:03:44.175 --> 00:03:46.435
That could be 90 to 100 miles an hour.

00:03:46.435 --> 00:03:49.086
You have a fraction of
a second, as a hitter,

00:03:49.086 --> 00:03:52.399
to identify if the pitch
is going to be a strike,

00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:54.026
and then we actually have to hit it.

00:03:55.611 --> 00:03:57.863
- I think this is going
to end very poorly for me.

00:03:59.103 --> 00:04:01.158
Nothing, woah!

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:04.286
- I just learned that these
balls can go well over

00:04:04.286 --> 00:04:06.705
100 miles per hour with
these professional pitchers.

00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:08.874
- [Woody] Dylan Axlerod,
starting pitcher with the

00:04:08.874 --> 00:04:10.167
Cincinnati Reds.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:11.171
- [Zach] Nothing that we did in the lab

00:04:11.171 --> 00:04:12.544
tells me I'm ready for this.

00:04:14.881 --> 00:04:16.298
- Oh, oh!

00:04:17.453 --> 00:04:18.460
That is fast.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.513
All right, here we go.

00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:22.721
- [Eugene] You can hear the
ball's friction in the air.

00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:25.391
It's like the ball's screaming
after it's been like spanked,

00:04:25.391 --> 00:04:26.308
you know.

00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:27.559
It's like, arrrggghhh!

00:04:29.259 --> 00:04:30.395
- (mumbles) this, Zach!

00:04:30.813 --> 00:04:32.189
- Oooohhh!

00:04:37.861 --> 00:04:40.781
- Argh! Argh! Yeah!

00:04:41.761 --> 00:04:43.075
- We made contact!

00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:45.185
- We made contact with the ball!

00:04:45.185 --> 00:04:47.246
- I think it's time to head
for the cool-down party.

00:04:47.246 --> 00:04:48.789
We'll focus on regeneration.

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:50.207
- What's the cool-down party?

00:04:50.207 --> 00:04:52.001
- All right, here we go.

00:04:53.411 --> 00:04:55.087
- What did we learn today?

00:04:55.087 --> 00:04:56.964
- Baseball is a hard sport.

00:04:56.964 --> 00:04:58.382
- It takes a lot of training.

00:04:58.382 --> 00:05:00.181
- Oh my God, this is cold.

00:05:00.181 --> 00:05:01.302
- I didn't hurt myself.

00:05:01.302 --> 00:05:02.892
This is like a huge win for me.

00:05:02.892 --> 00:05:03.982
- Oh my God.

00:05:03.982 --> 00:05:05.163
Cold on my butt.

00:05:06.223 --> 00:05:07.725
- This feels fantastic.

00:05:07.725 --> 00:05:08.859
- America's passtime.

00:05:08.859 --> 00:05:10.474
- People think that
baseball is a slow game,

00:05:10.474 --> 00:05:11.944
when you watch it on TV it feels slow.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:12.980
Ha-haa!

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.565
- There's a lot of athleticism involved.

00:05:14.565 --> 00:05:16.149
- Numbers and sports science.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.689
- You have to be so fit to do it.

00:05:17.689 --> 00:05:20.061
- It's so fast it just happened;
you blink and it's done.

00:05:20.061 --> 00:05:21.815
- Is it over?
- [Voiceover] You're done.

00:05:21.815 --> 00:05:22.864
- Thank goodness.

00:05:22.864 --> 00:05:24.116
- It's ending!

00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:26.743
♫ The cold never bothered me anyway ♫

00:05:26.817 --> 00:05:28.036
- [Voiceover] Today was crazy.

00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:30.622
Special thanks to P3
Peak Performance Project.

00:05:30.622 --> 00:05:31.456
- [Voiceover] The Lab.

00:05:31.456 --> 00:05:32.708
- [Voiceover] Westmont College Baseball.

00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:34.084
- [Voiceover] And all the
amazing players and coaches

00:05:34.084 --> 00:05:35.210
who helped us out.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.503
- [Voiceover] Until next time...

00:05:36.503 --> 00:05:39.090
- [All] What will we try next?!

00:05:41.346 --> 00:05:42.486
- Are we not doing that this time?

00:05:42.486 --> 00:05:43.547
- No, no, no.

00:05:43.547 --> 00:05:44.823
This was about baseball, not nudity.

